Yes—but love does not demand perfection or endless self-extraction. It demands that we stop hiding behind minimum compliance when we know we can offer real presence.

For those you love:

* listen past the first answer;
* say the difficult truth without cruelty;
* keep the promises that matter;
* repair quickly when you fail;
* protect time for them before only scraps remain;
* become more capable without making them pay for the becoming.

Drago’s correction: “more” is not always “better.” Sometimes love needs greater effort; sometimes it needs you to stop optimizing, put the hammer down, and simply be there.

Don’t be merely impressive for them. Be reliably available, honest, and alive with them. That is harder than excellence performed at a distance.